ing that  text into link there's a lot of white  space there like i have actually learned  a lot of words i haven't learned them by  flash guarding  um  so and this has been the case in in  these languages where it seems like  you'll never learn the words and then  then somehow these words are converted  into known words simply because you  spent so much time listening and reading  so  if i look at my arabic and persian i say  to myself i got all these words in  status one what can i do about it i'm  not gonna go flash card you know in in  persian 10 000 words most of which i  don't know  uh  i'm not going to go flash card  i'm just going to continue listing and  reading here's an interesting  transcript of a podcast self-help  podcast describing a book called deep  work or something or work deep i don't  remember just getting started into it  how to stay concentrated when you're  doing something  and this is interesting and i'm going to  do it in farsi persian and i'm going to  know most of the words  even though i have a limited vocabulary  because again the whole thing  when we deal with words we're dealing  with this rapid decline in word  frequency so that  i have enough words that i can  understand a lot of these contexts  continue to come across words that i saw  before but don't know when i looked them  up again  continue to encounter new words that i  look up and they become you know new  status one words and they're going to  reside in that status one  bucket for a long long time because they  may not show up again for a while but i  will continue doing interesting things  and gradually as has happened in all the  other languages that i have learned  gradually more and more of the language  more and more of the words  become known through this magical  process not because i deliberately tried  to flash card them but because  i saw them i saw them again i might move  them along manually and we may find a  way of doing this automatically that  after you've seen them more than a few  times it moves up until they become  status three words  and then the status three words you have  a good chance maybe you could flash card  those you might  do quite well on them because the whole  idea to me with flash cards is i don't  want to scratch my brain and get  frustrated on the other hand if i'm  getting  kind of exposure to things that i kind  of  60 70 percent know words phrases that i  sort of know and i see them again this  is all reinforcing and it's not  frustrating  so  uh the other thing too of course to  reinforce this idea that words are so  key  when i don't understand  in reading something it's not because i  don't understand the grammar that there  is a limited an amount of grammar to be  understood even if we can't produce it  correctly we understand that there are  cases in russian and there's an  inflection in  in other languages or subjunctive or  whatever it might be or  you know particles in japanese  but it's not the lack of grammar that  prevents me from understanding it's the  lack of words and the number of words is  enormous compared to the grammar rules  so to me language learning is all about  acquiring words  we can't be in a hurry to acquire the  words there is no shortcut to acquiring  the words  the bulk of the words that you meet  after a certain point are relatively low  frequency and they will stay in this  sort of new category at link and slowly  move up  to where they are ready to be launched  into your known word total some more  quickly than others but that's the  process and i guess that's the  conclusion that i come to  after analyzing my vocabulary statistics  at link  i invite you to do the same if you're on  link use those filters  and see just where your  new words are or where you're sorry  where your safe words are and how many  are  in status one two three and how many you  have learned and so forth and and the  main activity for me still is going to  be continuing to listen and read  plowing forward  and uh converting more blue  totally new words  into  you know status one  put them in the pipeline and eventually  they will move towards  known  okay that's what i wanted to say onwards  i look forward to your feedback
 

